These trade WebSocket frames are hand-built with synthetic values.
The ACK and CANCELLED order-response field shapes were informed by an
owner-authorized read-only observation on a funded subaccount. Their symbols,
ids, prices, quantities, and other values are made up; no raw live frame or
funded-account value is retained here. They prove parser behavior only and do
not establish venue acceptance.
The fill, open-orders, user-trades, and position examples are synthetic adaptations of
QFEX's published examples. The exchange reduce-only conversion is adapted from the
published order-response lifecycle example. Fee sign/currency and snapshot completeness
remain unknown.
